      "writtenOn": "2025-08-14T18:46:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The name \"pkvm_protect_setup\" sounds like there is some \"setup\", and this flags controls whether we should protect this setup or not. :)\n\nAnd the above comment is misleading (apart from being IMHO too detailed): not all steps needed for protection from host VM are completed: EPT is enabled on just one CPU, and IOMMU protection is rather not enabled at all?\n\nSo maybe something like e.g. `pkvm_setup_done`, and comment about what is actually important here (and not so obvious from the code), e.g.:\n\n```\n/*\n * This flag indicates, in particular, that the host EPT is set up\n * and is enabled on at least one CPU. It does *not* indicate yet\n * that pkvm is fully initialized.\n */\nstatic bool pkvm_setup_done __ro_after_init;\n```\n\nBTW \"is enabled on at least one CPU\" is important since, for example, if protect_pkvm_pages() succeeds (so the hypervisor memory is unmapped from the host EPT) but then create_iommu() fails, we return failure without setting this flag to true, so in pkvm_undo_finalise() we don\u0027t restore the mapping for the hypervisor memory in the host EPT, but that\u0027s ok since none of the CPUs has switched to this EPT.",
      "revId": "331b105cb9e8eb2d84bda4d54dab603764ef70c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
